From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0313-fog-04-macro-query-flush.patch

Source: 0313-fog-04-macro-query-flush.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches as 0193.

Port of zortos293/Lichii 7859ef4150 (2995da891 on port/ducky-oot-build16), Jonas.
Accurate GPU mode keeps report writes in the query cache until a fence, so
Ocarina's predicate macro 0x142 read a stale "visible" record. Does nothing while
the GPU split runs, as in the source. Ocarina on the PS5 runs the split with fast
GPU (run61), so it changes nothing there. Fast GPU is a launcher setting: Mario Kart
World had it off in runs 50 and 52, and on, with the split, in run45.

Switch: EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH=1, ours; the source has none. Default off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
  src/video_core/macro.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/macro.cpp b/src/video_core/macro.cpp
index e18e6c5a7f..eab0f9ee50 100644
--- a/src/video_core/macro.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/macro.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include "video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.h"
 #include "video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.h"
 #include "video_core/dirty_flags.h"
+#include "video_core/gpu_split.h"
 #include "video_core/memory_manager.h"
 #include "video_core/rasterizer_interface.h"
 #include "video_core/macro.h"
@@ -1509,6 +1510,17 @@ void MacroEngine::Execute(Core::System& system, Engines::Maxwell3D& maxwell3d, u
                             }
                         }
                     }
+                    // Accurate GPU mode holds report and semaphore writes in the query cache until a
+                    // fence: write them out, or occlusion predicates read stale values. The split only
+                    // runs with immediate payload writes, and the query cache belongs to its back.
+                    // EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH=1 turns this on.
+                    static const bool flush_queries = [] {
+                        const char* const flush = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_MACRO_QUERY_FLUSH");
+                        return flush != nullptr && flush[0] != '0';
+                    }();
+                    if (flush_queries && !VideoCommon::GpuSplit::Get().Active()) {
+                        memory.FlushRegion(source, read_bytes, VideoCommon::CacheType::QueryCache);
+                    }
                     if (memory.IsMemoryDirty(source, read_bytes, VideoCommon::CacheType::BufferCache)) {
                         memory.FlushRegion(source, read_bytes, VideoCommon::CacheType::BufferCache);
                         static u64 flushes{};
